// @reject: a string specifier is the trap that hid the disagreement: "hola" was
// @reject: true everywhere, so the engines looked like they agreed, while ""
// @reject: was false in the tree-walker and in the browser but true in the VM.
// @reject: Iterating a string's characters is `@ c:"hola"`, which is a different
// @reject: form and still works.
s = ""
@ s {
    >> "x" ¶
}
